From 0a6c4e7c6c92fec4c322a08705ee0f13fe5aadb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Hristov Yanev <icyhoty2k@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 22:18:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild history persistence: append-only, favorites, startup
 load
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ARCHITECTURE
  File is now append-only for new unique paths. Full rewrite only
  happens when toggling a favorite ('*' prefix must flip) or when
  clearing history (Delete key). This avoids rewriting 1000 lines
  on every folder navigation.

DATA MODEL
  HistoryFoldersManager gains:
    folderHistory  — MRU vector (index 0 = most recent), up to
                     HISTORY_MAX_DIRS_TO_SAVE entries.
    favorites      — unordered_set<wstring> for O(1) lookup.
                     Replaces per-scan searches through the vector.

FILE FORMAT (unchanged, backward-compatible)
  One path per line. Lines starting with '*' are favorites.
  File is oldest-first so new appends go to the bottom and
  LoadHistoryFromDisk() reverses to get MRU order in RAM.

STARTUP FIX
  UIManager::Init() calls LoadFolderHistoryFromDisk() (free function
  in UI namespace, same pattern as PushFolderHistory) before any
  folder is opened. This prevents the first PushFolderHistory from
  treating all saved paths as unknown and appending duplicates.

DISPLAY MODEL
  BuildDisplayList() assembles g_displayList (vector of DisplayEntry)
  from the MRU vector each time Show() is called or a key changes
  the list. Respects HISTORY_FAVORITES_POSITION (0=top, 1=bottom,
  2=in-place) and per-category caps (HISTORY_MAX_DIRS_TO_SHOW,
  HISTORY_MAX_FAVORITES_TO_SHOW). WM_PAINT and WM_KEYDOWN iterate
  g_displayList, not folderHistory directly.

FAVORITES (Space key — HISTORY_FAVORITES_TOGGLE_KEY)
  Toggles favorite on the hovered row. Rewrites file, rebuilds
  display list, resizes window to new row count, repaints.
  Favorite rows shown with gold star (U+2605) and warm text color.

CLEAR HISTORY (Delete key — HISTORY_CLEAR_ALL_HISTORY_BUT_NOT_FAVORITES)
  Removes all non-favorite entries from RAM and rewrites the file.
  Favorites survive. Hover reset to -1.
